{
  "tema": 6757,
  "slug": "gato-gata-toro-vaca",
  "titulo": "Gender of living creatures",
  "subtitulo": "El gato y la gata, el toro y la vaca.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "For people and animals, the female form is made in different ways: changing -o to -a (gato / gata), adding -a (león / leona), using a different word (toro / vaca), or keeping one word and changing only the article (el / la estudiante). Some animals have one gender for both sexes (la ballena, el tiburón): add macho or hembra.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Most change **-o** to **-a**: **el gato / la gata**, **el niño / la niña**, **el perro / la perra**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Many ending in a consonant add **-a**: **el león / la leona**, **el profesor / la profesora**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Pattern",
            "Male",
            "Female"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "-o → -a",
              "el gato",
              "la gata"
            ],
            [
              "+ -a",
              "el león",
              "la leona"
            ],
            [
              "other word",
              "el toro, el caballo, el hombre",
              "la vaca, la yegua, la mujer"
            ],
            [
              "only the article",
              "el estudiante, el turista",
              "la estudiante, la turista"
            ],
            [
              "one form for both",
              "la ballena, el tiburón",
              "la ballena, el tiburón"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With the last group, say **macho** or **hembra**: **la ballena macho**, **el tiburón hembra**. The article doesn't change."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Mi ==gata== duerme todo el día.",
              "en": "My (female) cat sleeps all day."
            },
            {
              "es": "==La yegua== y ==el caballo== están en el rancho.",
              "en": "The mare and the horse are at the ranch."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi tío tiene ==una vaca== y ==un toro==.",
              "en": "My uncle has a cow and a bull."
            },
            {
              "es": "==La estudiante== nueva es de Tecate.",
              "en": "The new (female) student is from Tecate."
            },
            {
              "es": "Vimos ==una ballena== cerca de Ensenada.",
              "en": "We saw a whale near Ensenada."
            },
            {
              "es": "Dicen que hay ==un tiburón hembra== en la bahía.",
              "en": "They say there's a female shark in the bay."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
